ought I''d pulled a muscle carrying my bag."},"variants":[{"when":{"vitals":{"spo2":{"below":88}}},"result":{"content":"Left calf… tight since the flight. Thought I''d… pulled it."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":["panic_attack","pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":"calf_symptom_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_anxiety_history","category":"ask","group":"Past medical & surgical history","label":"Ask about anxiety or panic attacks","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"Work has been stressful, but I''ve never had a panic attack or felt anything like this."},"variants":[{"when":{"vitals":{"spo2":{"below":88}}},"result":{"content":"Never… a panic attack. Never felt… anything like this."}}],"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":["panic_attack"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"check_vitals","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Repeat vital signs","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. She is anxious and speaking in short phrases."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["give_oxygen"],"vitals":{"spo2":{"below":92}}},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on high-flow oxygen, temperature {temp}°C. Even on oxygen she is struggling and speaks only in short phrases."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["give_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on supplemental oxygen, temperature {temp}°C. Still tachycardic, but more settled and managing fuller sentences."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["give_anxiolytic"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. Since the sedative she is drowsy, and her breathing is shallower but no less laboured."}},{"when":{"vitals":{"spo2":{"below":88}}},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. She is tiring: bolt upright, using her accessory muscles, managing only single words."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["pulmonary_embolism","panic_attack"],"against":["pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"examine_lungs","category":"examine","group":"Respiratory","label":"Examine the chest","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Air entry is equal. The lungs are clear without focal crackles or wheeze. Deep inspiration reproduces the pain."},"variants":[{"when":{"vitals":{"spo2":{"below":88}}},"result":{"content":"Air entry is equal and the lungs are still clear — no crackles or wheeze — despite her worsening hypoxaemia. She is using accessory muscles at {rr} breaths/min, and deep inspiration reproduces the pain."}}],"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":["pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"examine_legs","category":"examine","group":"Limbs & peripheral vascular","label":"Examine both legs","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Do not vigorously massage a limb when DVT is suspected.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The left calf is subtly fuller than the right and tender along the deep venous system. No cellulitis or injury is visible."},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":["panic_attack","pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":"dvt_signs_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"examine_heart","category":"examine","group":"Cardiovascular","label":"Examine the cardiovascular system","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Regular tachycardia at {hr} bpm. Heart sounds are normal, JVP is not elevated, and the peripheries are warm."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["pe_no_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"Regular tachycardia at {hr} bpm with a loud P2. The JVP is now raised and her hands are cool — her right ventricle is struggling."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_cxr","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Chest X-ray","timeCostMin":4,"moneyCost":85,"riskNote":"Low-dose ionising radiation.","result":{"type":"image","content":"The frontal chest radiograph is essentially normal: no focal consolidation, effusion, or pneumothorax. The lungs look far better than her oxygen saturation would suggest.","assetId":"pe_cxr_normal","annotation":{"xPercent":50,"yPercent":48,"radiusPercent":42,"label":"No focal air-space opacity"}},"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["pulmonary_embolism","panic_attack"],"against":["pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":"normal_cxr_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_ecg","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"12-lead ECG","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":45,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"ecg","content":"{rhythm} at {hr} bpm. Subtle T-wave inversion in V1 only; no ST elevation. The tracing is otherwise non-specific.","ecg":{"preset":"pe_early"},"annotation":{"xPercent":51.1,"yPercent":86.6,"radiusPercent":14,"label":"Regular narrow-complex tachycardia; no ST elevation"}},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["pe_no_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"{rhythm} at {hr} bpm with a new S1Q3T3 pattern, incomplete right bundle branch block and T-wave inversion in V1–V4: acute right ventricular strain. No ST elevation.","ecg":{"preset":"pe_rv_strain"},"annotation":{"xPercent":62.8,"yPercent":41.8,"radiusPercent":19,"label":"T-wave inversion V1–V3 (right ventricular strain)"}}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["pulmonary_embolism","panic_attack"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_bloods","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"D-dimer, troponin, FBC and CRP","timeCostMin":6,"moneyCost":110,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"The D-dimer is markedly elevated. Troponin is mildly raised, while inflammatory markers are normal.","labs":[{"test":"D-dimer","result":"3,480 ng/mL FEU","reference":"<500","flag":"high"},{"test":"High-sensitivity troponin","result":"28 ng/L","reference":"<14","flag":"high"},{"test":"WBC","result":"8.2 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"CRP","result":"3 mg/L","reference":"<5","flag":"normal"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["pe_no_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"The D-dimer is markedly elevated. Troponin has risen further, in keeping with right ventricular strain; inflammatory markers are normal.","labs":[{"test":"D-dimer","result":"3,620 ng/mL FEU","reference":"<500","flag":"high"},{"test":"High-sensitivity troponin","result":"64 ng/L","reference":"<14","flag":"high"},{"test":"WBC","result":"8.6 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"CRP","result":"3 mg/L","reference":"<5","flag":"normal"}]}}],"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":["panic_attack","pneumonia"],"triggersEvent":"d_dimer_positive","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_abg","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"Arterial blood gas","timeCostMin":4,"moneyCost":70,"riskNote":"Painful arterial puncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"On room air: hypoxaemia with respiratory alkalosis.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"7.48","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"high"},{"test":"PaO₂","result":"7.4 kPa","reference":"10.7–13.3","flag":"low"},{"test":"PaCO₂","result":"3.7 kPa","reference":"4.7–6.0","flag":"low"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"1.6 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"normal"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["give_anxiolytic"],"notAfterActions":["give_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"On room air after sedation: worse hypoxaemia, and the PaCO₂ has crept back to normal as she tires — falsely reassuring evidence of hypoventilation.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"7.40","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"normal"},{"test":"PaO₂","result":"6.6 kPa","reference":"10.7–13.3","flag":"low"},{"test":"PaCO₂","result":"5.0 kPa","reference":"4.7–6.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"2.1 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.