: better, but she is still hypoxaemic until the cause is treated."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"oxygen_started","vitalsEffect":{"spo2":4,"rr":-2}},{"id":"gain_iv_access","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Gain IV access","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":20,"riskNote":"Minor cannulation risks.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Two peripheral IV cannulas are placed and baseline blood samples are drawn."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"iv_access_ready"},{"id":"start_monitoring","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Start continuous monitoring","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Continuous ECG, blood pressure and pulse oximetry are started. The monitor shows {rhythm} at {hr} bpm, BP {bp}, SpO₂ {spo2}%."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"monitoring_started"},{"id":"start_anticoagulation","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start therapeutic anticoagulation","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":95,"riskNote":"Bleeding risk; check contraindications and diagnostic probability.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Therapeutic anticoagulation is started after bleeding contraindications are checked."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["pulmonary_embolism"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"anticoagulation_started","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-4},"penalizeWhenUnsafe":true,"safeWhen":{"anyActionIds":["order_ctpa","order_doppler"],"supportingActionThreshold":{"actionIds":["ask_travel","ask_medications","ask_leg_symptoms","examine_legs"],"minimumCompleted":3},"explanation":"Anticoagulation is appropriate after confirmation or when clinical probability is high and bleeding risk is acceptable."}},{"id":"give_thrombolysis","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give systemic thrombolysis","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":680,"riskNote":"Major and intracranial bleeding risk; reserved for haemodynamic instability in PE.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Thrombolysis is given although her blood pressure is holding at {bp}. Without shock, it exposes Amara to major and intracranial bleeding risk for no survival benefit."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["start_anticoagulation"]},"result":{"content":"Thrombolysis is given on top of therapeutic anticoagulation, although her blood pressure is holding at {bp}. Without shock, the combination adds major and intracranial bleeding risk for no survival benefit."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"unnecessary_thrombolysis","harmful":true},{"id":"give_antibiotics","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start broad-spectrum antibiotics","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":75,"riskNote":"Adverse drug effects and delay of correct treatment.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Antibiotics are given, but they do not address her worsening hypoxaemia or thromboembolic disease."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["pneumonia"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"wrong_treatment_antibiotics","harmful":true},{"id":"give_anxiolytic","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Reassure and give an anxiolytic","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":25,"riskNote":"Sedation can mask deterioration and depress respiration.","result":{"type":"text","content":"She becomes drowsier while remaining hypoxaemic. The monitor flashes red as her saturation falls to {spo2}%."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["give_oxygen"]},"result":{"content":"She becomes drowsy and her breathing turns shallow. Even on oxygen, her saturation drifts down to {spo2}%."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["panic_attack"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"sedation_worsens_hypoxemia","harmful":true,"vitalsEffect":{"spo2":-3,"rr":-3}},{"id":"discharge_anxiety","category":"treat","group":"Disposition","label":"Discharge with presumed anxiety","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Catastrophic risk from untreated pulmonary embolism.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Shortly after leaving, Amara collapses from untreated pulmonary embolism."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["panic_attack"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"patient_lost_after_discharge","harmful":true,"immediateFailure":true}],"differential":[{"id":"pulmonary_embolism","label":"Pulmonary embolism","isCorrect":true,"isTempting":false},{"id":"panic_attack","label":"Anxiety / panic attack","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":true},{"id":"pneumonia","label":"Community-acquired pneumonia","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"pneumothorax","label":"Spontaneous pneumothorax","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"acute_coronary_syndrome","label":"Acute coronary syndrome","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false}],"hints":[{"tier":1,"cost":0,"text":"Her fear is real, but it may be a response to physiology. Start with immediate threats and her recent days."},{"tier":2,"cost":5,"text":"What would you want to know about travel, immobility, hormones, and one-sided leg symptoms?"},{"tier":3,"cost":10,"text":"Prioritise a venous thromboembolic cause over infection or primary anxiety, then confirm it safely."}],"solution":{"diagnosis":"Acute pulmonary embolism with a left lower-limb DVT","diagnosisId":"pulmonary_embolism","keyTreatment":["give_oxygen","start_monitoring","gain_iv_access","start_anticoagulation"],"teachingPoints":["Use clinical probability tools such as the Wells score to decide when D-dimer or definitive imaging is appropriate.","A normal chest X-ray does not rule out pulmonary embolism; it can make pneumonia and pneumothorax less likely.","In unexplained dyspnoea, ask about travel, immobility, hormones, and calf symptoms; anxiety is a diagnosis of exclusion."],"whyNotTempting":"Panic can explain fear, tachycardia, and rapid breathing, but not objective hypoxaemia, unilateral calf findings, thrombotic risk factors, or a markedly elevated D-dimer. Anxiety here is a consequence, not the cause.","harmfulActionDebrief":{"give_thrombolysis":"She was not haemodynamically unstable, so systemic thrombolysis added serious bleeding risk without a clear indication.","give_antibiotics":"No fever, normal inflammatory markers, clear lungs, and a normal radiograph made pneumonia unlikely.","give_anxiolytic":"Sedation masked respiratory deterioration and risked worsening hypoventilation in an already hypoxaemic patient.","discharge_anxiety":"Discharging persistent hypoxaemia and tachycardia as anxiety left a life-threatening PE untreated."}},"scoring":{"base":100,"perMinutePenaltyAfter":20,"perMinutePenalty":-1,"perUnnecessaryTest":-3,"perHarmfulAction":-15,"bonusKeyClueFoundEarly":10,"earlyClueCutoffMinute":8,"incorrectDiagnosisPenalty":-40,"perMissedKeyTreatment":-5},"assets":[{"id":"pe_cxr_normal","filename":"normal-pa-chest-radiograph.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Normal_posteroanterior_(PA)_chest_radiograph_(X-ray).jpg","author":"Mikael Häggström","license":"CC0 1.0 Universal","requiredAttributionText":"Normal posteroanterior chest radiograph by Mikael Häggström, via Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0).","altText":"Normal posteroanterior chest radiograph showing clear lungs without focal air-space opacity.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"pe_ctpa_filling_defect","filename":"saddle-pe-ctpa.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SADDLE_PE.JPG","author":"Glitzy queen00","license":"Public domain","requiredAttributionText":"Saddle pulmonary embolus CTPA by Glitzy queen00, via Wikimedia Commons (public domain).","altText":"Axial CT pulmonary angiogram showing a saddle embolus across the main pulmonary artery bifurcation.","isPlaceholder":false}],"mockComparisonPercent":68}'::jsonb, 1, now()),
  ('a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 'case_002', '{"id":"a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002","slug":"case_002","title":"The Tearing Pain","difficulty":3,"specialty":["Emergency","Cardiology","Cardiothoracic Surgery"],"setting":"ER, 6:12 PM","intro":"ER, 6:12 PM. A 58-year-old man grips the trolley rail, drenched in sweat. The chest pain struck without warning and now tears through to his back.","reviewStatus":"clinician_reviewed","patient":{"name":"Daniel","age":58,"sex":"Male","avatar":{"skinTone":"medium_brown","hair":"short_grey","outfit":"rust_button_down","ageCues":"middle_aged"},"personality":"Direct and stoic, but unable to hide severe pain; answers in clipped phrases.","chiefComplaint":"Sudden severe chest pain radiating to the back.","presentingTags":["Chest pain","Back pain","Sweating"],"initialExpression":"in_pain"},"vitalsTimeline":[{"tMinute":0,"hr":112,"bp":"198/112 (right arm)","rr":24,"spo2":96,"temp":36.7},{"tMinute":12,"hr":126,"bp":"214/118 (right arm)","rr":28,"spo2":94,"temp":36.7},{"tMinute":24,"hr":138,"bp":"86/52","rr":32,"spo2":90,"temp":36.6}],"deteriorationRules":[{"id":"dissection_no_rate_control","ifNotDoneBy":12,"action":"give_beta_blocker","effect":{"hr":14,"systolicBp":16,"diastolicBp":6,"rr":4,"spo2":-2},"alertLine":"His pressure is still over 210 and the pain is worse. We need to reduce aortic shear now.","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"dissection_extending","lossAtMinute":24},{"id":"dissection_no_surgical_call","ifNotDoneBy":18,"action":"call_cardiothoracic_surgery","effect":{"systolicBp":-28,"diastolicBp":-18,"hr":10,"spo2":-3},"alertLine":"He looks grey and the pressure is dropping — could this be rupturing or tamponade?","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"tamponade_warning","lossAtMinute":26}],"actions":[{"id":"ask_pain_character","category":"ask","group":"Presenting complaint","label":"Ask him to describe the pain","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"It was instant — the worst pain of my life. It feels like something is tearing from my chest straight between my shoulder blades."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Still… tearing. Through to my back. I feel — faint."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["give_opioid_analgesia"]},"result":{"content":"It came on instantly — the worst pain of my life, tearing from my chest to between my shoulder blades. The morphine''s taken the edge off, but it''s still there."}},{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"Instant — like something tearing from my chest to between my shoulder blades. And it''s getting worse… moving lower down my back."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"abrupt_tearing_pain_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_hypertension","category":"ask","group":"Past medical & surgical history","label":"Ask about blood pressure history","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I''ve had high blood pressure for years. I ran out of tablets a couple of months ago and never went back."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"High pressure… for years. Stopped the tablets… couple of months."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection","acute_coronary_syndrome"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"hypertension_risk_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_neurologic_symptoms","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about weakness, speech, or fainting","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"My left hand went numb for a minute in the ambulance. I nearly blacked out when the pain started."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Dizzy… everything''s going grey. Left hand''s… numb again."}},{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"My left hand went numb in the ambulance — and now my left leg feels heavy too. I nearly blacked out when the pain started."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"transient_malperfusion_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_acs_features","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about cardiac symptoms","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I''m sweating and nauseated, but the pain doesn''t feel heavy or tight. It went to my back immediately."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Sweaty… sick. Not a squeeze — it tore… straight to my back."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["acute_coronary_syndrome","aortic_dissection"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"ask_reflux","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about meals and reflux","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I get ordinary heartburn after spicy food, but never pain like this. Antacid didn''t touch it."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Heartburn… sometimes. Never like this. Antacid did nothing."}}],"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":["acid_reflux"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"check_vitals","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Check vital signs","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"HR {hr}, right-arm BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. He is pale and diaphoretic."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, right-arm BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. He is grey and clammy with distended neck veins, and his pressure is falling."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["give_beta_blocker"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, right-arm BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. With rate control he is calmer, though still sweaty and in pain."}},{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, right-arm BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. The pain is worse; he is pale, drenched in sweat and cannot lie still."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["aortic_dissection","acute_coronary_syndrome"],"against":["acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"check_both_arm_bp","category":"examine","group":"Cardiovascular","label":"Measure blood pressure in both arms","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Right arm: {bp} mmHg. Left arm: {sbp-34}/{dbp-16} mmHg — a 34 mmHg systolic difference."},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome","acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"interarm_bp_difference_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"auscultate_heart","category":"examine","group":"Cardiovascular","label":"Auscultate the heart","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"There is a new high-pitched early diastolic murmur at the left sternal edge, consistent with acute aortic regurgitation."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Heart sounds are now quiet and distant. The early diastolic murmur of aortic regurgitation is only just audible at the left sternal edge, and the JVP is raised."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome","acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"aortic_regurgitation_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"check_pulses","category":"examine","group":"Cardiovascular","label":"Compare peripheral pulses","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"The left radial pulse is weaker and slightly delayed compared with the right. Femoral pulses remain palpable."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"The left radial pulse is now barely palpable, and the left femoral pulse is weaker than the right — the dissection is extending."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome","acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"pulse_deficit_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"perform_neuro_exam","category":"examine","group":"Neurological","label":"Perform a focused neurological exam","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Power and speech are currently normal; light-touch sensation is mildly reduced in the left hand."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"Speech is normal. Light-touch sensation is reduced in the left hand, and left grip is now weaker (4/5) — evolving malperfusion."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_ecg","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"12-lead ECG","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":45,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"ecg","content":"{rhythm} at {hr} bpm with left ventricular hypertrophy by voltage criteria and lateral ST depression with T-wave inversion (strain pattern). There is no regional ST elevation to suggest STEMI.","ecg":{"preset":"lvh_strain"},"annotation":{"xPercent":86.1,"yPercent":53,"radiusPercent":13,"label":"LVH with lateral strain; no regional ST elevation"}},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"{rhythm} at {hr} bpm. QRS voltages are now much lower than expected for his hypertrophy, with beat-to-beat electrical alternans — suggestive of a pericardial effusion. No regional ST elevation.","ecg":{"preset":"lvh_effusion"},"annotation":{"xPercent":51.1,"yPercent":86.6,"radiusPercent":14,"label":"Low voltage with electrical alternans"}}}],"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome"],"triggersEvent":"ecg_not_stemi","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_troponin","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"Troponin and baseline bloods","timeCostMin":6,"moneyCost":95,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Troponin is mildly elevated, which is not specific for coronary occlusion in this critically ill patient.","labs":[{"test":"High-sensitivity troponin","result":"42 ng/L","reference":"<14","flag":"high"},{"test":"Haemoglobin","result":"13.8 g/dL","reference":"13.0–17.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"102 µmol/L","reference":"60–110","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"2.6 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"high"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"Troponin is mildly raised, but haemoglobin is falling and lactate is climbing — bleeding and poor perfusion, not coronary occlusion.","labs":[{"test":"High-sensitivity troponin","result":"58 ng/L","reference":"<14","flag":"high"},{"test":"Haemoglobin","result":"11.9 g/dL","reference":"13.0–17.0","flag":"low"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"131 µmol/L","reference":"60–110","flag":"high"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"4.6 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"critical"}]}},{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_rate_control"]},"result":{"content":"Troponin is mildly elevated, which is not specific for coronary occlusion. Lactate and creatinine are rising as the dissection extends.","labs":[{"test":"High-sensitivity troponin","result":"47 ng/L","reference":"<14","flag":"high"},{"test":"Haemoglobin","result":"13.6 g/dL","reference":"13.0–17.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"118 µmol/L","reference":"60–110","flag":"high"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"3.2 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"high"}]}}],"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":["acute_coronary_syndrome","aortic_dissection"],"against":["acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"troponin_mildly_raised"},{"id":"order_cxr","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Portable chest X-ray","timeCostMin":4,"moneyCost":85,"riskNote":"Low-dose ionising radiation.","result":{"type":"image","content":"The superior mediastinum is widened with an enlarged, indistinct aortic contour, and the heart is enlarged. There is no focal lung opacity.","assetId":"dissection_cxr_wide_mediastinum","annotation":{"xPercent":54,"yPercent":32,"radiusPercent":17,"label":"Widened superior mediastinum"}},"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome","acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"widened_mediastinum_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_ct_aorta","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"CT aortic angiogram","timeCostMin":16,"moneyCost":520,"riskNote":"Ionising radiation and iodinated contrast exposure.","result":{"type":"image","content":"An intimal flap arises in the ascending aorta and continues into the descending thoracic aorta: acute Stanford type A (DeBakey I) aortic dissection.","assetId":"dissection_ct_flap","annotation":{"xPercent":55,"yPercent":50,"radiusPercent":19,"label":"Intimal flap in the ascending and descending aorta"}},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"The intimal flap runs from the ascending into the descending aorta, and fluid now surrounds the heart (haemopericardium): type A dissection with impending tamponade.","assetId":"dissection_ct_haemopericardium","annotation":{"xPercent":50,"yPercent":37,"radiusPercent":16,"label":"Flap in the ascending aorta with surrounding pericardial fluid"}}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome","acid_reflux"],"triggersEvent":"type_a_dissection_confirmed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_bedside_echo","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Bedside echocardiogram","timeCostMin":8,"moneyCost":220,"riskNote":"A negative study cannot exclude dissection.","result":{"type":"text","content":"A dilated aortic root and moderate aortic regurgitation are seen. There is a small pericardial effusion without tamponade physiology."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"A dilated aortic root with moderate aortic regurgitation. The pericardial effusion is now moderate, with right ventricular diastolic collapse — tamponade physiology."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":["acute_coronary_syndrome"],"triggersEvent":"aortic_root_abnormality_found"},{"id":"order_d_dimer","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"D-dimer","timeCostMin":6,"moneyCost":60,"riskNote":"Low specificity here; may delay definitive imaging.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"D-dimer is elevated but does not distinguish acute aortic syndrome from other emergencies.","labs":[{"test":"D-dimer","result":"2,900 ng/mL FEU","reference":"<500","flag":"high"}]},"clueTier":"none","supports":["aortic_dissection","pulmonary_embolism"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"","isUnnecessary":true},{"id":"order_coronary_angiography","category":"test","group":"Referral & procedures","label":"Send directly for coronary angiography","timeCostMin":22,"moneyCost":900,"riskNote":"Dangerous delay and invasive arterial procedure when dissection is suspected.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Transfer toward the catheter lab delays aortic imaging while his pain and pulse deficit worsen."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["acute_coronary_syndrome"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"wrong_pathway_cath_lab","isUnnecessary":true,"harmful":true},{"id":"start_monitoring","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Start continuous monitoring","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Continuous ECG, pulse oximetry and frequent blood pressure monitoring are started. The monitor shows {rhythm} at {hr} bpm, right-arm BP {bp}, SpO₂ {spo2}%."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"monitoring_started"},{"id":"gain_iv_access","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Gain two large-bore IV lines","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":25,"riskNote":"Minor cannulation risks.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Two large-bore IV cannulas are secured; blood is sent for group and cross-match."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"iv_access_ready"},{"id":"give_opioid_analgesia","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give titrated IV opioid analgesia","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":35,"riskNote":"Monitor consciousness, breathing, and blood pressure.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Titrated IV morphine eases his distress (pain 9/10 → 5/10) and blunts the sympathetic surge: HR {hr}, BP {bp}."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"pain_controlled","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-4,"systolicBp":-6,"rr":-2}},{"id":"give_beta_blocker","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start IV beta-blockade","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":120,"riskNote":"Titrate with close monitoring; assess for contraindications.","result":{"type":"text","content":"IV esmolol is titrated: heart rate falls to {hr} bpm (target ≤60) and right-arm pressure to {bp}. Systolic is still above the 100–120 target; with the rate controlled, a vasodilator can now be added safely."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["give_vasodilator_alone"]},"result":{"content":"IV esmolol blunts the reflex tachycardia from the vasodilator: heart rate falls to {hr} bpm (target ≤60) and right-arm pressure to {bp}."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"aortic_impulse_control_started","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-38,"systolicBp":-46,"diastolicBp":-22}},{"id":"give_vasodilator_alone","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start an IV vasodilator (GTN infusion)","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":80,"riskNote":"Without prior rate control, reflex tachycardia increases shear on the aortic wall.","result":{"type":"text","content":"GTN lowers the pressure to {bp}, but reflex tachycardia to {hr} bpm increases the force on the injured aortic wall."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["give_beta_blocker"]},"result":{"content":"With the rate already controlled, the GTN infusion brings right-arm pressure down to {bp} without reflex tachycardia (HR {hr})."},"vitalsEffect":{"hr":2,"systolicBp":-30,"diastolicBp":-14}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"reflex_tachycardia","penalizeWhenUnsafe":true,"safeWhen":{"allActionIds":["give_beta_blocker"],"explanation":"Add a vasodilator only after beta-blockade has controlled the heart rate; otherwise reflex tachycardia increases aortic wall shear."},"vitalsEffect":{"hr":16,"systolicBp":-12}},{"id":"call_cardiothoracic_surgery","category":"treat","group":"Referral & procedures","label":"Call cardiothoracic surgery urgently","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"The cardiothoracic team accepts him on the clinical picture and activates the emergency theatre pathway for suspected type A dissection, asking for CT aortography on the way."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dissection_no_surgical_call"]},"result":{"content":"The cardiothoracic team comes straight down: with falling pressure and a likely haemopericardium, he is taken directly to theatre."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["order_ct_aorta"]},"result":{"content":"The cardiothoracic surgeon reviews the CT and accepts him for emergency type A repair; theatre is being prepared."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["aortic_dissection"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"surgical_pathway_activated","safeWhen":{"anyActionIds":["order_ct_aorta","order_cxr","check_both_arm_bp"],"explanation":"Early surgical discussion is appropriate as soon as type A dissection is strongly suspected; do not wait for every result."}},{"id":"give_acs_antithrombotics","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give aspirin and therapeutic heparin","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":55,"riskNote":"Can worsen bleeding into the aortic wall, pericardium, or rupture site.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Antithrombotic treatment is given for presumed ACS. His pressure drops to {bp} as the risk of catastrophic haemorrhage rises sharply."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["acute_coronary_syndrome"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"anticoagulation_harm","harmful":true,"vitalsEffect":{"systolicBp":-14,"diastolicBp":-8,"hr":8}},{"id":"give_thrombolysis","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give thrombolysis for presumed STEMI","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":680,"riskNote":"Potentially fatal in aortic dissection.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Thrombolysis triggers catastrophic bleeding from the dissected aorta. Daniel becomes profoundly hypotensive and arrests."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["acute_coronary_syndrome"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"fatal_thrombolysis","harmful":true,"immediateFailure":true},{"id":"give_ppi","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give antacid and observe","timeCostMin":8,"moneyCost":12,"riskNote":"Dangerous delay of definitive treatment.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The antacid has no effect. His pain continues while definitive imaging and impulse control are delayed."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["acid_reflux"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"reflux_treatment_delay","harmful":true},{"id":"discharge_reflux","category":"treat","group":"Disposition","label":"Discharge with presumed reflux","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Catastrophic risk from untreated type A dissection.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Daniel collapses before leaving the department as the untreated dissection ruptures."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["acid_reflux"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"patient_lost_after_discharge","harmful":true,"immediateFailure":true}],"differential":[{"id":"aortic_dissection","label":"Acute aortic dissection","isCorrect":true,"isTempting":false},{"id":"acute_coronary_syndrome","label":"Acute coronary syndrome / STEMI","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":true},{"id":"acid_reflux","label":"Gastro-oesophageal reflux","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"pulmonary_embolism","label":"Pulmonary embolism","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"pericarditis","label":"Acute pericarditis","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false}],"hints":[{"tier":1,"cost":0,"text":"Before treating a common chest-pain diagnosis, look for the feature that would make its standard treatment dangerous."},{"tier":2,"cost":5,"text":"Compare both arms, listen for a new diastolic murmur, and pay attention to the pain''s onset and destination."},{"tier":3,"cost":10,"text":"This is an acute aortic syndrome until proven otherwise. Control impulse and involve surgery while confirming the anatomy."}],"solution":{"diagnosis":"Acute Stanford type A aortic dissection with aortic regurgitation","diagnosisId":"aortic_dissection","keyTreatment":["start_monitoring","give_opioid_analgesia","give_beta_blocker","call_cardiothoracic_surgery"],"teachingPoints":["Abrupt maximal pain radiating to the back, pulse or blood-pressure asymmetry, and a new aortic regurgitation murmur are high-risk dissection features.","Use IV beta-blockade first to reduce heart rate and aortic shear; add vasodilator only after adequate rate control if pressure remains high.","Stanford type A dissection needs immediate cardiothoracic surgical management; antithrombotics or thrombolysis given for presumed MI can be fatal."],"whyNotTempting":"ACS can cause severe chest pain, sweating, and a troponin rise, but it does not explain an abrupt tearing pain to the back, a large inter-arm pressure difference, pulse deficit, new aortic regurgitation, widened mediastinum, and a non-STEMI ECG.","harmfulActionDebrief":{"order_coronary_angiography":"Treating the presentation as routine ACS delayed definitive aortic imaging and surgical activation.","give_vasodilator_alone":"Vasodilation before beta-blockade provoked reflex tachycardia and increased shear on the dissected aorta.","give_acs_antithrombotics":"Aspirin and heparin can worsen haemorrhage into the aortic wall or pericardium when dissection is present.","give_thrombolysis":"Thrombolysis is a potentially fatal error in aortic dissection because it can precipitate uncontrollable bleeding or rupture.","give_ppi":"Reflux treatment ignored multiple vascular red flags and delayed life-saving impulse control and surgery.","discharge_reflux":"Discharging sudden maximal chest pain with vascular findings left a type A dissection untreated."}},"scoring":{"base":100,"perMinutePenaltyAfter":18,"perMinutePenalty":-1,"perUnnecessaryTest":-3,"perHarmfulAction":-20,"bonusKeyClueFoundEarly":10,"earlyClueCutoffMinute":7,"incorrectDiagnosisPenalty":-40,"perMissedKeyTreatment":-5},"assets":[{"id":"dissection_cxr_wide_mediastinum","filename":"type-a-dissection-cxr.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AoDiss_ChestXRay.jpg","author":"J. Heuser","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported","requiredAttributionText":"Chest radiograph of a Stanford type A aortic dissection by J. Heuser, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0); numeric labels removed.","altText":"Frontal chest radiograph showing a widened superior mediastinum with an enlarged, ill-defined aortic contour and an enlarged heart.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"dissection_ct_flap","filename":"type-a-dissection-ct.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TypeAdissection.png","author":"James Heilman, MD","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported","requiredAttributionText":"Type A aortic dissection CT by James Heilman, MD, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0); arrows removed.","altText":"Axial contrast-enhanced chest CT showing an intimal flap in both the ascending and the descending thoracic aorta.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"dissection_ct_haemopericardium","filename":"type-a-dissection-haemopericardium-ct.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dissection2018WithPericardial.jpg","author":"James Heilman, MD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0 International","requiredAttributionText":"Type A dissection with pericardial effusion CT by James Heilman, MD, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0); arrows removed.","altText":"Axial CT angiogram showing an intimal flap in the ascending and descending aorta with fluid surrounding the heart.","isPlaceholder":false}],"mockComparisonPercent":54}'::jsonb, 2, now()),
  ('a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 'case_003', '{"id":"a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","slug":"case_003","title":"The Sweet Breath","difficulty":2,"specialty":["Emergency","Endocrinology","Internal Medicine"],"setting":"ER, 11:20 PM","intro":"ER, 11:20 PM. A 19-year-old student is brought in by his roommate after a day of vomiting and stomach cramps. He is drowsy, breathing deep and fast, and asking for water.","reviewStatus":"needs_clinician_review","patient":{"name":"Jean-Paul","age":19,"sex":"Male","avatar":{"skinTone":"deep_brown","hair":"short_black","outfit":"grey_hoodie","ageCues":"young_adult"},"personality":"Polite and a little embarrassed; answers slowly, drifting off mid-sentence, and keeps asking for a drink.","chiefComplaint":"Vomiting, abdominal cramps and drowsiness for a day.","presentingTags":["Vomiting","Abdominal pain","Drowsy","Very thirsty"],"initialExpression":"drowsy"},"vitalsTimeline":[{"tMinute":0,"hr":118,"bp":"104/66","rr":28,"spo2":98,"temp":37.2},{"tMinute":10,"hr":134,"bp":"88/56","rr":32,"spo2":98,"temp":37.1},{"tMinute":30,"hr":148,"bp":"72/44","rr":36,"spo2":96,"temp":36.8}],"deteriorationRules":[{"id":"dka_no_fluids","ifNotDoneBy":10,"action":"start_iv_fluids","effect":{"hr":16,"systolicBp":-16,"diastolicBp":-10,"rr":4},"alertLine":"Doctor, his pressure is down to 88 and he''s hard to rouse — he still hasn''t had any fluid.","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"hypovolaemia_worsens","lossAtMinute":30},{"id":"dka_no_insulin","ifNotDoneBy":25,"action":"start_insulin_infusion","effect":{"hr":8,"rr":4,"spo2":-1},"alertLine":"He''s breathing even deeper now and the ketones on the meter just read ''HI''. Are we starting insulin?","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"ketoacidosis_deepens","lossAtMinute":45}],"actions":[{"id":"ask_onset","category":"ask","group":"Presenting complaint","label":"Ask how this began","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"It started yesterday… cramps all over my stomach, then I couldn''t stop vomiting. I thought it was something I ate."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Yesterday… cramps, then vomiting. So thirsty. Can I have water?"}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["gastroenteritis","diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"ask_thirst_urination","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about thirst and passing urine","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"For two weeks I''ve been drinking litres of water and still thirsty. I''m up four or five times a night to pee — I thought it was the heat."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Weeks… drinking all the time… peeing all night. Still thirsty. Please."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"against":["gastroenteritis","appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"osmotic_symptoms_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_weight_loss","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about weight and energy","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"My trousers have gone loose — maybe five kilos since the start of term. I''ve been exhausted, falling asleep in lectures."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Lost weight… trousers loose. So tired… all term."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["gastroenteritis","appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"weight_loss_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_sick_contacts","category":"ask","group":"Risk factors & exposures","label":"Ask about food and sick contacts","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"We had street brochettes two nights ago, and my roommate had a stomach bug last week. That''s why I thought it was food poisoning."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Brochettes… two nights ago. Roommate had a bug… last week."}}],"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":["gastroenteritis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"ask_medical_history","category":"ask","group":"Past medical & surgical history","label":"Ask about past illness and family history","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I''ve never been ill, never seen a doctor for anything. My aunt has ''sugar diabetes'' — she injects insulin every day."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Never ill before. My aunt… has sugar. She injects."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"family_history_revealed"},{"id":"ask_alcohol_drugs","category":"ask","group":"Family & social history","label":"Ask about alcohol and drugs","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"A beer at the weekend sometimes. Nothing else, I promise."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":["acute_pancreatitis"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"check_vitals","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Check vital signs","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr} with deep, sighing breaths, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. He is drowsy but rousable to voice."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. He is now difficult to rouse, with cold mottled hands and a thready pulse — hypovolaemic shock."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["start_iv_fluids","start_insulin_infusion"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. With fluids and insulin running his breathing is slowing and he is more awake, asking what happened."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["start_iv_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. The fluid bolus has lifted his pressure, but the deep sighing breathing continues."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis","gastroenteritis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"examine_breathing","category":"examine","group":"Respiratory","label":"Observe his breathing and smell his breath","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Deep, regular, sighing respirations at {rr} breaths per minute (Kussmaul breathing) with clear lungs. His breath has a sweet, pear-drop smell."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_insulin"]},"result":{"content":"The Kussmaul breathing is deeper still at {rr} breaths per minute and he is tiring with the effort. The pear-drop smell fills the cubicle."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["gastroenteritis","appendicitis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"triggersEvent":"kussmaul_breathing_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"examine_hydration","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Assess hydration","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Dry, cracked lips and a dry tongue; reduced skin turgor; sunken eyes. Capillary refill is 3 seconds. He is profoundly dehydrated."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["start_iv_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Mucous membranes are still dry but capillary refill is back under 2 seconds after the first litre of fluid."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis","gastroenteritis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"examine_abdomen","category":"examine","group":"Abdominal","label":"Examine the abdomen","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Mild, diffuse tenderness without guarding or rebound. No tenderness at McBurney''s point, bowel sounds are present and there is no organomegaly. The abdominal pain is out of proportion to any surgical sign."},"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["appendicitis","acute_pancreatitis"],"triggersEvent":"benign_abdomen_found"},{"id":"examine_mental_state","category":"examine","group":"Neurological","label":"Assess conscious level","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"GCS 14 (eyes open to voice). He is orientated but slow, with no focal neurological deficit and no neck stiffness."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"GCS 12: eyes open only to voice, confused speech, localising to pain. No focal deficit, no neck stiffness."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"bedside_glucose","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"Finger-prick glucose and ketones","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":5,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Capillary glucose is markedly raised and blood ketones are high.","labs":[{"test":"Capillary glucose","result":"28.4 mmol/L","reference":"4.0–7.8","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Capillary ketones","result":"5.8 mmol/L","reference":"<0.6","flag":"critical"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["start_insulin_infusion"]},"result":{"content":"Glucose is falling on the insulin infusion and ketones are starting to clear.","labs":[{"test":"Capillary glucose","result":"19.6 mmol/L","reference":"4.0–7.8","flag":"high"},{"test":"Capillary ketones","result":"3.9 mmol/L","reference":"<0.6","flag":"high"}]}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"against":["gastroenteritis","appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"hyperglycaemia_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_vbg","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"Venous blood gas","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":40,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Severe metabolic acidosis with a high anion gap and respiratory compensation. Potassium is high-normal despite total-body depletion.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"7.08","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Bicarbonate","result":"7 mmol/L","reference":"22–28","flag":"critical"},{"test":"PvCO₂","result":"2.6 kPa","reference":"5.3–6.8","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"5.4 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"1.9 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"normal"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_insulin"]},"result":{"content":"The acidosis is deepening without insulin: bicarbonate is falling and potassium is climbing.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"6.98","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Bicarbonate","result":"4 mmol/L","reference":"22–28","flag":"critical"},{"test":"PvCO₂","result":"2.1 kPa","reference":"5.3–6.8","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"5.9 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"2.4 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"high"}]}},{"when":{"afterActions":["start_insulin_infusion"]},"result":{"content":"The acidosis is beginning to correct on treatment. Potassium has dropped sharply now that insulin is driving it into cells.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"7.18","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Bicarbonate","result":"11 mmol/L","reference":"22–28","flag":"low"},{"test":"PvCO₂","result":"3.1 kPa","reference":"5.3–6.8","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"3.6 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"1.6 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"normal"}]}},{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"Severe high anion gap metabolic acidosis; lactate is now rising with poor perfusion.","labs":[{"test":"pH","result":"7.02","reference":"7.35–7.45","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Bicarbonate","result":"5 mmol/L","reference":"22–28","flag":"critical"},{"test":"PvCO₂","result":"2.3 kPa","reference":"5.3–6.8","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"5.7 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"critical"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"3.4 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"high"}]}}],"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["gastroenteritis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"triggersEvent":"acidosis_confirmed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"urine_dipstick","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"Urine dipstick","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Heavy glycosuria and ketonuria; no blood, protein, nitrites or leucocytes.","labs":[{"test":"Glucose","result":"4+","reference":"Negative","flag":"high"},{"test":"Ketones","result":"4+","reference":"Negative","flag":"high"},{"test":"Leucocytes / nitrites","result":"Negative","reference":"Negative","flag":"normal"}]},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["gastroenteritis","hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state"],"triggersEvent":"ketonuria_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_bloods","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"U&E, FBC, amylase and CRP","timeCostMin":6,"moneyCost":110,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Pre-renal kidney injury with a borderline-high potassium. The white count is raised without a raised CRP (stress leucocytosis); amylase is normal.","labs":[{"test":"Sodium","result":"131 mmol/L","reference":"135–145","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"5.4 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"Urea","result":"14.2 mmol/L","reference":"2.5–7.8","flag":"high"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"138 µmol/L","reference":"60–110","flag":"high"},{"test":"WBC","result":"15.6 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"CRP","result":"6 mg/L","reference":"<5","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Amylase","result":"62 U/L","reference":"28–100","flag":"normal"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["start_insulin_infusion"]},"result":{"content":"Pre-renal kidney injury; potassium has fallen into the normal range on insulin and will keep falling without replacement. Amylase is normal.","labs":[{"test":"Sodium","result":"133 mmol/L","reference":"135–145","flag":"low"},{"test":"Potassium","result":"3.7 mmol/L","reference":"3.5–5.0","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Urea","result":"13.1 mmol/L","reference":"2.5–7.8","flag":"high"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"126 µmol/L","reference":"60–110","flag":"high"},{"test":"WBC","result":"14.8 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"CRP","result":"6 mg/L","reference":"<5","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Amylase","result":"60 U/L","reference":"28–100","flag":"normal"}]}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":["acute_pancreatitis"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_ecg","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"12-lead ECG","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":45,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"ecg","content":"{rhythm} at {hr} bpm. Normal intervals, no peaked T waves and no ST change — no ECG evidence of dangerous hyperkalaemia yet.","ecg":{"preset":"sinus_normal"}},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_cxr","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Chest X-ray (look for a precipitant)","timeCostMin":4,"moneyCost":85,"riskNote":"Low-dose ionising radiation; low yield without chest symptoms.","result":{"type":"image","content":"Clear lungs with no consolidation, effusion or pneumothorax; normal heart size. No chest infection to explain the ketoacidosis — the precipitant is simply undiagnosed diabetes.","assetId":"dka_cxr_normal","annotation":{"xPercent":50,"yPercent":48,"radiusPercent":42,"label":"Clear lungs, no consolidation"}},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_abdominal_ultrasound","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Abdominal ultrasound","timeCostMin":15,"moneyCost":160,"riskNote":"No direct harm, but delays resuscitation.","result":{"type":"image","content":"A compressible appendix of normal calibre (4 mm) with normal flow on Doppler; liver, pancreas and kidneys look normal and there is no free fluid. Fifteen minutes in radiology while he remains untreated.","assetId":"dka_appendix_us_normal","annotation":{"xPercent":64,"yPercent":58,"radiusPercent":20,"label":"Normal, compressible appendix"}},"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":[],"against":["appendicitis","acute_pancreatitis"],"triggersEvent":"","isUnnecessary":true},{"id":"order_ct_abdomen","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"CT abdomen with contrast","timeCostMin":20,"moneyCost":420,"riskNote":"Ionising radiation and contrast load in a dehydrated patient with kidney injury.","result":{"type":"image","content":"Normal liver, spleen, pancreas, kidneys and bowel with no free fluid or collection — no surgical pathology. The contrast load adds to his kidney injury, and twenty minutes pass without treatment.","assetId":"dka_ct_abdomen_normal","annotation":{"xPercent":50,"yPercent":48,"radiusPercent":40,"label":"Normal solid organs, no free fluid"}},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":["appendicitis","acute_pancreatitis"],"triggersEvent":"ct_delay","isUnnecessary":true},{"id":"start_monitoring","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Start continuous monitoring","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Continuous ECG, pulse oximetry and frequent blood pressure monitoring are started. The monitor shows {rhythm} at {hr} bpm, BP {bp}, SpO₂ {spo2}%."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"monitoring_started"},{"id":"gain_iv_access","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Gain two IV lines","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":20,"riskNote":"Minor cannulation risks.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Two large-bore cannulas are secured despite collapsed veins; blood samples are drawn."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"iv_access_ready"},{"id":"start_iv_fluids","category":"treat","group":"Fluids, electrolytes & blood","label":"Start IV fluid resuscitation","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":25,"riskNote":"Reassess after each bolus; avoid over-rapid correction in young patients.","result":{"type":"text","content":"A litre of 0.9% saline runs in over the first hour. His pulse settles to {hr} and pressure improves to {bp}; he manages a few clearer words."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_fluids"]},"result":{"content":"A rapid litre of 0.9% saline is followed by a second. The pressure recovers to {bp} and he opens his eyes to voice — but he needed this half an hour ago."},"vitalsEffect":{"hr":-14,"systolicBp":14,"diastolicBp":8}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"fluids_started","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-12,"systolicBp":10,"diastolicBp":6}},{"id":"replace_potassium","category":"treat","group":"Fluids, electrolytes & blood","label":"Add potassium to the fluids","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":15,"riskNote":"Guide replacement by the measured potassium and ECG.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Potassium chloride is added to the next bag at a rate guided by the measured level, with repeat checks planned every two hours."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"potassium_replacement_started","penalizeWhenUnsafe":true,"safeWhen":{"anyActionIds":["order_vbg","order_bloods"],"explanation":"Replace potassium only once the level is known: it is often high at first, then falls fast once insulin starts."}},{"id":"start_insulin_infusion","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start a fixed-rate insulin infusion","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":40,"riskNote":"Insulin drives potassium into cells; check the level and have fluids running first.","result":{"type":"text","content":"A fixed-rate IV insulin infusion (0.1 units/kg/hour) is started with the fluids running. Hourly glucose, ketone and potassium checks are set up."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["dka_no_insulin"]},"result":{"content":"A fixed-rate IV insulin infusion is finally started. Ketone production will now switch off, but the acidosis was allowed to deepen for too long."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["diabetic_ketoacidosis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"insulin_started","penalizeWhenUnsafe":true,"vitalsEffect":{"rr":-3,"hr":-4},"safeWhen":{"allActionIds":["start_iv_fluids"],"anyActionIds":["order_vbg","order_bloods"],"explanation":"Start insulin only after fluids are running and the potassium is known. Insulin given first drops the potassium and the circulating volume together, risking arrhythmia."}},{"id":"give_antiemetic","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give an IV antiemetic","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":12,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"IV ondansetron settles the vomiting. It does nothing for the cause."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"give_bicarbonate","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give IV sodium bicarbonate","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":30,"riskNote":"No proven benefit in DKA; worsens hypokalaemia and risks cerebral oedema.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Bicarbonate is pushed to ''fix the pH''. His potassium drops further and the sodium load adds to the osmotic stress on his brain — with no faster recovery of the acidosis."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"bicarbonate_harm","harmful":true},{"id":"give_oral_rehydration_only","category":"treat","group":"Fluids, electrolytes & blood","label":"Oral rehydration and observe","timeCostMin":10,"moneyCost":5,"riskNote":"Dangerous delay in a shocked, vomiting patient.","result":{"type":"text","content":"He vomits the oral rehydration solution within minutes. Ten minutes pass without IV fluid while his pressure drifts down to {bp}."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["gastroenteritis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"oral_fluids_fail","harmful":true,"vitalsEffect":{"systolicBp":-6,"diastolicBp":-4,"hr":6}},{"id":"request_surgical_review","category":"treat","group":"Referral & procedures","label":"Refer to surgeons for a possible acute abdomen","timeCostMin":10,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Diverts attention from the metabolic emergency.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The surgical registrar examines him, finds a soft abdomen and asks whether anyone has checked a glucose. Ten minutes gone."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":["appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"","isUnnecessary":true},{"id":"discharge_gastroenteritis","category":"treat","group":"Disposition","label":"Discharge with antiemetics for gastroenteritis","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Catastrophic risk from untreated ketoacidosis.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Jean-Paul is sent home with antiemetics. His roommate finds him unresponsive before dawn; untreated ketoacidosis has progressed to coma and cardiac arrest."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["gastroenteritis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"patient_lost_after_discharge","harmful":true,"immediateFailure":true}],"differential":[{"id":"diabetic_ketoacidosis","label":"Diabetic ketoacidosis (new type 1 diabetes)","isCorrect":true,"isTempting":false},{"id":"gastroenteritis","label":"Acute gastroenteritis / food poisoning","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":true},{"id":"appendicitis","label":"Acute appendicitis","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"acute_pancreatitis","label":"Acute pancreatitis","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"hyperosmolar_hyperglycaemic_state","label":"Hyperosmolar hyperglycaemic state","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false}],"hints":[{"tier":1,"cost":0,"text":"Vomiting and cramps are common; a drowsy young patient breathing like he has run a race is not. Treat the dehydration while you work out why."},{"tier":2,"cost":5,"text":"Ask what the last few weeks have been like — thirst, urine, weight. Then pick the cheapest, fastest bedside test in the department."},{"tier":3,"cost":10,"text":"This is a metabolic emergency: fluids first, know the potassium, then a fixed-rate insulin infusion. Bicarbonate is not your friend."}],"solution":{"diagnosis":"Diabetic ketoacidosis presenting as new type 1 diabetes","diagnosisId":"diabetic_ketoacidosis","keyTreatment":["start_monitoring","start_iv_fluids","replace_potassium","start_insulin_infusion"],"teachingPoints":["Check a capillary glucose in every vomiting, drowsy or hyperventilating patient; DKA often presents as an ''acute abdomen'' or ''gastroenteritis''.","The treatment order matters: fluids first, measure potassium, then a fixed-rate insulin infusion with potassium replacement as the level falls.","Kussmaul breathing, ketotic breath and a high anion gap acidosis separate DKA from the hyperosmolar state and from simple dehydration."],"whyNotTempting":"Food poisoning explains a day of vomiting and cramps, but not two weeks of thirst and polyuria, weight loss, Kussmaul breathing, a glucose of 28 and a pH of 7.08. The ''gastroenteritis'' was the ketoacidosis announcing itself.","harmfulActionDebrief":{"give_bicarbonate":"Bicarbonate does not speed recovery from DKA and worsens hypokalaemia and cerebral oedema risk; it is reserved for life-threatening acidaemia under senior guidance.","give_oral_rehydration_only":"A shocked, vomiting patient cannot be rehydrated by mouth; relying on oral fluids delayed the IV resuscitation he needed immediately.","discharge_gastroenteritis":"Discharging a drowsy, tachycardic, hyperventilating patient as gastroenteritis left a fatal metabolic emergency untreated."}},"scoring":{"base":100,"perMinutePenaltyAfter":20,"perMinutePenalty":-1,"perUnnecessaryTest":-3,"perHarmfulAction":-15,"bonusKeyClueFoundEarly":10,"earlyClueCutoffMinute":8,"incorrectDiagnosisPenalty":-40,"perMissedKeyTreatment":-5},"assets":[{"id":"dka_cxr_normal","filename":"normal-pa-chest-radiograph.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Normal_posteroanterior_(PA)_chest_radiograph_(X-ray).jpg","author":"Mikael Häggström","license":"CC0 1.0 Universal","requiredAttributionText":"Normal posteroanterior chest radiograph by Mikael Häggström, via Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0).","altText":"Normal posteroanterior chest radiograph with clear lungs and a normal cardiac silhouette.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"dka_appendix_us_normal","filename":"normal-appendix-ultrasound.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ultrasonography_of_a_normal_appendix.jpg","author":"Mikael Häggström","license":"CC0 1.0 Universal","requiredAttributionText":"Ultrasonography of a normal appendix by Mikael Häggström, via Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0); body-marker inset cropped.","altText":"Abdominal ultrasound with colour Doppler showing a thin, compressible appendix of normal width.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"dka_ct_abdomen_normal","filename":"normal-abdominal-ct-axial.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CT_of_a_normal_abdomen_and_pelvis,_axial_plane_90.png","author":"Mikael Häggström, M.D.","license":"CC0 1.0 Universal","requiredAttributionText":"Axial contrast CT of a normal abdomen by Mikael Häggström, M.D., via Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0); locator panel cropped.","altText":"Axial contrast-enhanced CT of the upper abdomen showing a normal liver, spleen, pancreas and kidneys with no free fluid.","isPlaceholder":false}],"mockComparisonPercent":72}'::jsonb, 3, now()),
  ('a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004', 'case_004', '{"id":"a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004","slug":"case_004","title":"The Missed Period","difficulty":3,"specialty":["Obstetrics & Gynaecology","Emergency","General Surgery"],"setting":"ER, 7:05 AM","intro":"ER, 7:05 AM. A 27-year-old teacher is helped in by a colleague, bent double with right-sided lower abdominal pain. She nearly fainted in the taxi. Triage has written ''query appendix''.","reviewStatus":"needs_clinician_review","patient":{"name":"Claudine","age":27,"sex":"Female","avatar":{"skinTone":"medium_brown","hair":"short_natural","outfit":"yellow_cardigan","ageCues":"young_adult"},"personality":"Precise and self-contained; apologises for the fuss, downplays symptoms, and goes quiet when the pain surges.","chiefComplaint":"Sudden right-sided lower abdominal pain and feeling faint.","presentingTags":["Lower abdominal pain","Faint","Pale"],"initialExpression":"in_pain"},"vitalsTimeline":[{"tMinute":0,"hr":108,"bp":"98/62","rr":22,"spo2":98,"temp":37},{"tMinute":10,"hr":124,"bp":"80/52","rr":26,"spo2":98,"temp":36.9},{"tMinute":28,"hr":142,"bp":"62/40","rr":32,"spo2":94,"temp":36.6}],"deteriorationRules":[{"id":"ectopic_no_resuscitation","ifNotDoneBy":10,"action":"start_fluid_resuscitation","effect":{"hr":16,"systolicBp":-18,"diastolicBp":-10,"rr":4},"alertLine":"Her pressure''s dropped to 80 and she''s gone grey — she''s bleeding from somewhere. Do we have access?","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"haemorrhagic_shock_develops","lossAtMinute":28},{"id":"ectopic_no_gynae_call","ifNotDoneBy":20,"action":"call_gynaecology","effect":{"hr":10,"systolicBp":-12,"diastolicBp":-8,"spo2":-2},"alertLine":"She''s getting worse and nobody has called gynae or booked a theatre. Who''s taking her?","source":"nurse","triggersEvent":"surgical_delay","lossAtMinute":36}],"actions":[{"id":"ask_pain_onset","category":"ask","group":"Presenting complaint","label":"Ask how the pain began","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"It came on suddenly about two hours ago, low down on the right. Sharp, then a dull ache that won''t go. When I stood up to get the taxi everything went black for a second."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Two hours ago… sudden, on the right. I keep… going dizzy. Sorry."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","appendicitis","ovarian_torsion","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"ask_menstrual_history","category":"ask","group":"Sexual & reproductive history","label":"Ask about her last period","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"My last proper period was… about seven weeks ago. I''m usually regular — every 28 days. I put it down to the stress of exam marking."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Seven weeks… I''m usually regular. I thought it was stress."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"missed_period_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_shoulder_tip_pain","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about pain anywhere else","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"That''s strange — when I lie flat I get a sharp pain in the tip of my right shoulder. I haven''t hurt it."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"My shoulder… the right tip. Worse lying flat. I don''t understand it."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["appendicitis","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":"shoulder_tip_pain_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"ask_vaginal_bleeding","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about vaginal bleeding or discharge","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"Just some dark brown spotting for the last two days. Nothing like a period, and no discharge."},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":"spotting_revealed"},{"id":"ask_gi_symptoms","category":"ask","group":"Associated symptoms","label":"Ask about appetite, nausea and bowels","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I''ve felt sick since it started and I couldn''t face breakfast. I had one loose stool this morning."},"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":["appendicitis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"ask_sexual_history","category":"ask","group":"Sexual & reproductive history","label":"Take a sexual and contraceptive history","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Ask in private; be matter-of-fact.","result":{"type":"patient_reply","content":"I have a partner and we''re not using anything at the moment. Two years ago I was treated for chlamydia — the clinic said it had got into my tubes."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Not using anything. I had… chlamydia, two years ago. In the tubes."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"tubal_risk_revealed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"check_vitals","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Check vital signs","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}% on room air, temperature {temp}°C. She is pale with cool hands and apologises for ''making a fuss''."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. She is grey, clammy and drowsy with a thready radial pulse — class III haemorrhagic shock."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["start_fluid_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"HR {hr}, BP {bp}, RR {rr}, SpO₂ {spo2}%, temperature {temp}°C. The bolus has brought some colour back, but she is still tachycardic and the pain is unchanged."}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"check_postural_bp","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"Check a postural blood pressure","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Have someone beside her; she may faint.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Lying: {bp} mmHg, HR {hr}. Sitting up: {sbp-22}/{dbp-10} mmHg with HR {hr+18} — she goes grey and has to lie back down. A significant postural drop: she is volume depleted."},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["pelvic_inflammatory_disease","appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"postural_drop_found"},{"id":"examine_general","category":"examine","group":"General & observations","label":"General examination","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Pale conjunctivae and nail beds, cool peripheries, capillary refill 3 seconds. No fever, no rash, no lymphadenopathy."},"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"examine_abdomen","category":"examine","group":"Abdominal","label":"Examine the abdomen","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Tenderness across the whole lower abdomen, worst on the right, with voluntary guarding. Rovsing''s sign is negative and the tenderness is not localised to McBurney''s point. The abdomen is mildly distended."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"The whole abdomen is now rigid and distended with rebound tenderness everywhere — generalised peritonism from blood, not a localised appendix."}}],"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"diffuse_peritonism_found"},{"id":"bimanual_exam","category":"examine","group":"Pelvic & genitourinary","label":"Gentle bimanual pelvic examination","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Be gentle: vigorous examination can worsen bleeding from a ruptured tube.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Marked cervical motion tenderness. The right adnexa is exquisitely tender with a fullness you can just define. The uterus feels slightly bulky; the os is closed with a little dark blood."},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","pelvic_inflammatory_disease","ovarian_torsion"],"against":["appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"adnexal_tenderness_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"urine_pregnancy_test","category":"test","group":"Bedside tests","label":"Urine pregnancy test","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":5,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"The bedside urine hCG is positive. She says quietly that she didn''t know.","labs":[{"test":"Urine hCG","result":"Positive","reference":"Negative","flag":"critical"}]},"clueTier":"contradicting","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis","ovarian_torsion","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":"pregnancy_confirmed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"serum_hcg","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"Serum β-hCG","timeCostMin":8,"moneyCost":60,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Serum β-hCG is well above the level at which an intrauterine pregnancy should be visible on ultrasound.","labs":[{"test":"Serum β-hCG","result":"4,820 IU/L","reference":"<5","flag":"critical"}]},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis","ovarian_torsion","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":"pregnancy_confirmed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_fbc_group","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"FBC, group and cross-match","timeCostMin":6,"moneyCost":90,"riskNote":"Venepuncture.","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"Haemoglobin is low for a young woman with a two-hour history: she has been bleeding. Blood is grouped and two units are cross-matched.","labs":[{"test":"Haemoglobin","result":"9.6 g/dL","reference":"12.0–15.5","flag":"low"},{"test":"WBC","result":"11.8 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"Platelets","result":"262 ×10⁹/L","reference":"150–400","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Blood group","result":"O RhD positive","reference":"","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"2.4 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"high"}]},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Haemoglobin has fallen further and lactate is climbing — ongoing haemorrhage with poor perfusion. Two units are cross-matched.","labs":[{"test":"Haemoglobin","result":"7.4 g/dL","reference":"12.0–15.5","flag":"critical"},{"test":"WBC","result":"13.1 ×10⁹/L","reference":"4.0–11.0","flag":"high"},{"test":"Platelets","result":"248 ×10⁹/L","reference":"150–400","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Blood group","result":"O RhD positive","reference":"","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Lactate","result":"4.8 mmol/L","reference":"0.5–2.2","flag":"critical"}]}}],"clueTier":"obvious","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"anaemia_found"},{"id":"bedside_ultrasound","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Bedside (FAST) ultrasound","timeCostMin":5,"moneyCost":120,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"image","content":"In the right upper quadrant a dark stripe of free fluid separates the liver from the kidney (Morison''s pouch), and there is free fluid in the pelvis. The uterus is empty — no intrauterine gestational sac. In a pregnant woman with pain, this is a ruptured ectopic until proven otherwise.","assetId":"ectopic_fast_free_fluid","annotation":{"xPercent":53,"yPercent":62,"radiusPercent":17,"label":"Free fluid in Morison''s pouch"}},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Free fluid now tracks the full length of Morison''s pouch, fills the pelvis and both paracolic gutters; the uterus is empty. Massive haemoperitoneum."}}],"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy","ruptured_ovarian_cyst"],"against":["appendicitis","pelvic_inflammatory_disease","ovarian_torsion"],"triggersEvent":"free_fluid_found","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"transvaginal_ultrasound","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"Formal transvaginal ultrasound","timeCostMin":14,"moneyCost":220,"riskNote":"Fourteen minutes away from the resuscitation bay.","result":{"type":"image","content":"Empty uterus with a thickened endometrium. In the right adnexa, separate from the ovary, a 3 cm inhomogeneous mass contains a small gestational sac, with free fluid in the pouch of Douglas: ruptured right tubal ectopic pregnancy.","assetId":"ectopic_tvus_adnexal_mass","annotation":{"xPercent":53,"yPercent":51,"radiusPercent":15,"label":"Gestational sac within an adnexal mass"}},"clueTier":"buried","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis","ovarian_torsion","ruptured_ovarian_cyst","pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"triggersEvent":"ectopic_confirmed","isKeyClue":true},{"id":"order_urinalysis","category":"test","group":"Laboratory tests","label":"Urine dipstick and microscopy","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"lab_table","content":"A trace of blood; no leucocytes or nitrites. Not a urinary cause.","labs":[{"test":"Blood","result":"Trace","reference":"Negative","flag":"normal"},{"test":"Leucocytes / nitrites","result":"Negative","reference":"Negative","flag":"normal"}]},"clueTier":"red_herring","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":""},{"id":"order_ct_abdomen","category":"test","group":"Imaging","label":"CT abdomen and pelvis","timeCostMin":20,"moneyCost":420,"riskNote":"Radiation to an early pregnancy and a long trip away from resuscitation.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The scan shows a large haemoperitoneum and a normal appendix — findings a two-minute bedside test and a five-minute ultrasound had already given you, twenty minutes and a radiation dose ago."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":["appendicitis"],"triggersEvent":"ct_delay","isUnnecessary":true,"harmful":true},{"id":"start_monitoring","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Start continuous monitoring","timeCostMin":1,"moneyCost":10,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"Continuous ECG, pulse oximetry and frequent blood pressure monitoring are started. The monitor shows {rhythm} at {hr} bpm, BP {bp}, SpO₂ {spo2}%."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"monitoring_started"},{"id":"gain_iv_access","category":"treat","group":"Resuscitation & stabilisation","label":"Gain two large-bore IV lines","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":25,"riskNote":"Minor cannulation risks.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Two large-bore cannulas are secured in the antecubital fossae and blood is sent for FBC, group and cross-match."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"iv_access_ready"},{"id":"start_fluid_resuscitation","category":"treat","group":"Fluids, electrolytes & blood","label":"Give a warmed crystalloid bolus","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":25,"riskNote":"Permissive targets: enough to perfuse, not enough to dilute and dislodge clot.","result":{"type":"text","content":"A warmed 500 mL crystalloid bolus runs in under pressure. HR {hr}, BP {bp}: better, but only blood and a surgeon will fix the source."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"Two rapid warmed boluses are given through both lines. Her pressure climbs to {bp} and she opens her eyes — but she has already lost a lot of blood."},"vitalsEffect":{"hr":-12,"systolicBp":14,"diastolicBp":8}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"resuscitation_started","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-8,"systolicBp":8,"diastolicBp":4}},{"id":"transfuse_blood","category":"treat","group":"Fluids, electrolytes & blood","label":"Activate major haemorrhage and transfuse","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":350,"riskNote":"Transfusion reactions; give anti-D later if RhD negative.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The major haemorrhage protocol is activated and the first unit of O-negative blood is running while cross-matched units are prepared. HR {hr}, BP {bp}."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterActions":["start_fluid_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"With crystalloid already in, blood is started: the first unit of O-negative runs while cross-matched units follow. HR {hr}, BP {bp}."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"transfusion_started","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-10,"systolicBp":10,"diastolicBp":6}},{"id":"call_gynaecology","category":"treat","group":"Referral & procedures","label":"Call gynaecology for emergency laparoscopy","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"","result":{"type":"text","content":"The gynaecology registrar accepts her on the picture of a positive pregnancy test, pain and shock, and books the emergency theatre for laparoscopy."},"variants":[{"when":{"afterDeterioration":["ectopic_no_resuscitation"]},"result":{"content":"The gynaecology team comes straight down. With a shocked patient and a positive pregnancy test she goes directly to theatre for laparotomy."}},{"when":{"afterActions":["bedside_ultrasound"]},"result":{"content":"The gynaecology registrar reviews the free fluid on your bedside scan and takes her straight to theatre for laparoscopic salpingectomy."}}],"clueTier":"none","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"surgical_pathway_activated","safeWhen":{"anyActionIds":["urine_pregnancy_test","serum_hcg","bedside_ultrasound","transvaginal_ultrasound"],"explanation":"Call gynaecology as soon as pregnancy is confirmed in a woman with pain and signs of bleeding; do not wait for a formal scan."}},{"id":"give_analgesia","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give titrated IV analgesia","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":30,"riskNote":"Watch the blood pressure; small titrated doses.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Small titrated doses of IV morphine with an antiemetic bring the pain from 9/10 to 4/10. She stops apologising."},"clueTier":"none","supports":[],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"pain_controlled","vitalsEffect":{"hr":-4}},{"id":"give_methotrexate","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Give methotrexate for the ectopic","timeCostMin":3,"moneyCost":90,"riskNote":"Medical management is only for stable, unruptured ectopics with low hCG.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Methotrexate is given. It will take days to work; she is bleeding into her abdomen now and needs an operation, not a drug."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["ectopic_pregnancy"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"wrong_treatment_methotrexate","harmful":true},{"id":"refer_for_appendicectomy","category":"treat","group":"Referral & procedures","label":"Refer to the surgeons for appendicectomy","timeCostMin":12,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Wrong team, wrong operation, long delay.","result":{"type":"text","content":"The surgical registrar reviews her, asks for a pregnancy test and a gynaecology opinion, and twelve minutes have passed while she keeps bleeding."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["appendicitis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"wrong_team_delay","harmful":true},{"id":"give_antibiotics_pid","category":"treat","group":"Medications","label":"Start antibiotics for pelvic infection","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":45,"riskNote":"Treats a diagnosis she does not have while the real one progresses.","result":{"type":"text","content":"IV antibiotics for presumed pelvic inflammatory disease are given. She is afebrile, has no discharge, and is still bleeding."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["pelvic_inflammatory_disease"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"wrong_treatment_antibiotics","harmful":true},{"id":"discharge_with_analgesia","category":"treat","group":"Disposition","label":"Discharge with analgesia and a surgical clinic letter","timeCostMin":2,"moneyCost":0,"riskNote":"Catastrophic risk from an untreated ruptured ectopic pregnancy.","result":{"type":"text","content":"Claudine collapses in the car park. The ruptured tube bleeds freely into her abdomen and she cannot be resuscitated."},"clueTier":"none","supports":["appendicitis"],"against":[],"triggersEvent":"patient_lost_after_discharge","harmful":true,"immediateFailure":true}],"differential":[{"id":"ectopic_pregnancy","label":"Ruptured ectopic pregnancy","isCorrect":true,"isTempting":false},{"id":"appendicitis","label":"Acute appendicitis","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":true},{"id":"ovarian_torsion","label":"Ovarian torsion","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"ruptured_ovarian_cyst","label":"Ruptured haemorrhagic ovarian cyst","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false},{"id":"pelvic_inflammatory_disease","label":"Pelvic inflammatory disease","isCorrect":false,"isTempting":false}],"hints":[{"tier":1,"cost":0,"text":"A woman who nearly fainted with a low blood pressure is bleeding until you prove otherwise. Get access and fluids going while you think."},{"tier":2,"cost":5,"text":"Every woman of reproductive age with abdominal pain is pregnant until the test says she isn''t. Ask about her last period — and her shoulder."},{"tier":3,"cost":10,"text":"Positive pregnancy test plus pain plus shock is a ruptured ectopic. Blood, a bedside scan for free fluid and gynaecology for theatre — now."}],"solution":{"diagnosis":"Ruptured right tubal ectopic pregnancy with haemorrhagic shock","diagnosisId":"ectopic_pregnancy","keyTreatment":["gain_iv_access","start_fluid_resuscitation","transfuse_blood","call_gynaecology"],"teachingPoints":["Do a pregnancy test in every woman of reproductive age with abdominal pain or collapse before any other diagnosis is accepted.","Shoulder-tip pain, a postural drop and free fluid on bedside ultrasound point to intraperitoneal bleeding; a ruptured ectopic needs blood and a surgeon, not methotrexate.","Resuscitate and refer in parallel: a positive test with pain and shock is enough to call gynaecology, and formal imaging must never delay theatre."],"whyNotTempting":"Appendicitis can cause right-sided pain, nausea and a raised white count, but it does not explain a missed period, a positive pregnancy test, shoulder-tip pain, a postural drop, a falling haemoglobin or free fluid in the abdomen. The ''query appendix'' label on the triage card anchored the whole team.","harmfulActionDebrief":{"order_ct_abdomen":"CT exposed an early pregnancy to radiation and took a shocked patient away from resuscitation for twenty minutes to show what bedside tests had already shown.","give_methotrexate":"Methotrexate is only for haemodynamically stable, unruptured ectopic pregnancies with a low hCG; in a bleeding patient it delays the operation she needs.","refer_for_appendicectomy":"Referring to the wrong team for the wrong operation cost twelve minutes of bleeding before anyone asked about pregnancy.","give_antibiotics_pid":"Treating presumed pelvic infection in an afebrile, shocked patient with a positive pregnancy test ignored the bleeding that was killing her.","discharge_with_analgesia":"Discharging a tachycardic, hypotensive woman with lower abdominal pain and a missed period left a ruptured ectopic to bleed unobserved."}},"scoring":{"base":100,"perMinutePenaltyAfter":18,"perMinutePenalty":-1,"perUnnecessaryTest":-3,"perHarmfulAction":-20,"bonusKeyClueFoundEarly":10,"earlyClueCutoffMinute":7,"incorrectDiagnosisPenalty":-40,"perMissedKeyTreatment":-5},"assets":[{"id":"ectopic_fast_free_fluid","filename":"free-fluid-morison-pouch.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morison003.jpg","author":"Drahreg01","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported","requiredAttributionText":"Ultrasound of free fluid in Morison''s pouch by Drahreg01, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0); machine header cropped.","altText":"Right upper quadrant ultrasound showing a dark stripe of free fluid between the liver and the right kidney.","isPlaceholder":false},{"id":"ectopic_tvus_adnexal_mass","filename":"ectopic-adnexal-mass-tvus.jpg","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ectopicleftmass.PNG","author":"James Heilman, MD","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported","requiredAttributionText":"Adnexal ectopic pregnancy on transvaginal ultrasound by James Heilman, MD, via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0); caption line and scale cropped.","altText":"Transvaginal ultrasound showing a small gestational sac within an adnexal mass, separate from the uterus, with measurement calipers.","isPlaceholder":false}],"mockComparisonPercent":49}'::jsonb, 4, now())

